From a56a6ed9bbc0ad23d244a9e4d6b83a9f0e8cc8b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:58:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The enum default sweep: a miss returned Hans

An enum with no default= encodes defaultInt 0, and EnumOps pushes `value ?? defaultInt`
- so a MISS RETURNS 0, NOT NULL. That is what made the skillcape emote breathe dragonfire
at anyone in a plain cape on 2026-09-12, and the note then said it was worth a repo-wide
sweep. This is that sweep.

Id 0 is a real, plausible thing in every table where it matters:

    seq.pack:0       swarm_walk
    spotanim.pack:0  triple_firebreath_attack
    npc.pack:0       hans
    obj.pack:0       mcannonremains
    loc.pack:0       mcannoncrate

61 enums across 18 files output one of those types and had no default=. All 61 now have
default=null. The 96 enums that output int, string, coord or boolean are untouched - a 0
there is ordinary and usually intended, and flagging them would bury the ones that matter.

TWO LIVE BUGS FALL OUT OF IT, and in both cases the guard was already written correctly.
The enum was lying to it.

  * slayer_superior. superiors.rs2 reads the task's superior and tests `if ($superior =
    null | $killed = $superior) { return; }`. task_name.enum has 84 slayer tasks and
    superiors.enum has 15, so on the other 69 the lookup missed and answered npc 0 - which
    is Hans. With Bigger and Badder unlocked, every on-task kill on one of those 69 tasks
    was one 1/200 roll away from `npc_add(npc_coord, hans, 200); npc_setmode(opplayer2)`
    and "@red@A superior foe has appeared...". Hans, the Lumbridge greeter, attacking you
    for two minutes.

  * skillcape_grimy_herb. brew_potion.rs2 tests `if ($clean ! null)` on a Herblore cape
    wearer's used item. Any non-herb used on a vial of water answered mcannonremains and
    passed the guard.

Both are fixed by the default alone; neither call site needed changing.

Also fixed, found in the same read: npc_combat.rs2 tested `%magearena > ^mage_arena_complete`
where mage_arena_bosses runs 0..5 and ^mage_arena_complete is 6. So the moment the demon
died the whole Kolodion block was entered and fell PAST the "you have already proven
yourself" test into the "you must now fight him as" messages - which then indexed
mage_arena_boss_names at 6 and missed as well. States 7 and 8 were handled correctly; 6,
the state every finisher sits in until they pray at the statue, was not. Now >=.

RULE 17 in rs2check makes it permanent: an enum whose outputtype has a real id 0 must
declare default=. And poh_mutate gains mutation 44 to prove the rule fires - because the
first version of rule 17 used the HEADER regex, which requires a comma and therefore never
matches a config block header, so it reported nothing at all when a default= was deleted.
That is the second rule in this file to ship inert. Break the thing a new rule is meant to
catch, every time.

poh_furniture.enum and poh_tablets.enum are generated, so the default goes in genfurn.py
and gentablets.py rather than the output - poh_battery check 38/43 catches the difference,
which is how that was noticed.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK over 1,663 scripts and 456 configs, poh_battery ALL PASS,
poh_mutate 44/44 caught, rs2check --selftest PASS. Not compiled.

